Ladybird sizes an image without a natural size against the canvas when
drawing it, as Blink and WebKit do. Blink’s Canvas2DRecorderContext
passes the canvas’s Width() and Height() to ElementSize() as the default
object size, which for an SVG image gives SVGImageForContainer::
ConcreteObjectSize(), and WebKit’s CanvasRenderingContext2DBase passes
canvasBase().size() to size(). Gecko instead falls back to 300 by 150
for a missing dimension, in nsLayoutUtils::SurfaceFromElement(), but it
draws such an image all the same.
